WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.580
So I have a pet dog in this game...

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.310
...and it's so cute that I start talking to it.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.300
You know how...

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.470
...when you talk to animals...

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.550
...your voice gets all syrupy?

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.230
Except this was in a game.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.560
I know what you mean.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.850
When I talk to my goldfish...

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.980
...I lapse into baby talk.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.770
I get talking to dogs and cats...

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.230
...but people who talk to fish must be pretty darn lonely.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.030
What did you say?!

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.740
That's discrimination!

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.570
What's with the patronizing look?!

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:02.450
Oh, yeah.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.660
I've been wondering for a while...

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.110
When people call hot dogs...

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:07.910
...wieners...

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.950
I wonder what that means.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.210
U-Um...

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.290
It would take a long time if I went into detail...

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.960
...but it was definitely derived from a German word.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.720
Okay.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.220
Raise your hand if you just thought of something naughty.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.020
Oh, yeah...

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.190
Gu***m is still ridiculously popular.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.610
